## FORMULAS & CALCULATIONS

[calc-00002] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: For variance or percentage change calculations (e.g., (Q3-Q2)/Q2), always use conditional logic to handle zero-denominators: use `np.where(q2 == 0, 'NA', (q3 - q2) / q2)` to prevent `#DIV/0!` errors.
## CODE SNIPPETS & TEMPLATES

[code-00001] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When generating Excel files, use a single, self-contained Python block with `xlsxwriter` or `openpyxl`. The script must include all data, logic, and a final `df.to_excel()` or `writer.save()` call to disk. Do not truncate code; ensure the script is fully runnable.
